    "done_when": "For each metered budget group and role, reckon/budget.py reports the runs remaining before the weekly reset. The figure is the group's remaining seven-day window divided by the mean per-run quota cost over the trailing seven days. The per-run cost is read from the committed run records' lane_receipt quota_windows, which carry a ten-thousand-and-eighty-minute window. The figure carries its own observation age, and it is unmeasured, never zero, when fewer than one priced run exists. The judgement extends _group_bar and group_pace rather than adding a second bar. The drain deadline comes from reckon/crew/pace.py, and group membership from budget_group.declared_groups; neither is restated. A wave whose projected cost, its node count times the mean per-run cost, exceeds the remaining window is refused, and the refusal names the runs remaining and the reset time. Exposing the figure on the command line is out of scope. tests/test_preflight_runs_remaining.py builds synthetic run records and a synthetic group window under tmp_path. It asserts the runs-remaining figure, the refusal of a wave projected past its reset with the runs-remaining figure and reset time in its text, admission of a wave inside the window, and unmeasured when no priced run exists. It passes at exit 0, as do the existing budget and pace test files the change reaches. The manifest records base and head arms of those files, each log header printing its revision and reckon.__file__, with FAILED ids per arm, and cites the reuse map at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s25-coord/s25-reuse-map-quota-runway/reuse-map.md section 1, re-derived at its own base. The declared negative control is applied, the past-reset wave is observed to be admitted, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED test id.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
